<title>USA: NeXstar says FDA approval sought for drug.</title>
<headline>NeXstar says FDA approval sought for drug.</headline>
<dateline>BOULDER, Colo. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>NeXstar Pharmaceuticals Inc said Monday that its U.S. marketing and development partner, Fujisawa USA Inc, has submitted a new drug application to the Food and Drug Administration for AmBisome for injection.</p>
<p>The application seeks approval of AmBisome for injection as a primary treatment for confirmed and presumptive fungal infections and for visceral leishmaniasis, a parasitic infection.</p>
<p>It also seeks approval for the treatment of fungal infections refractory to amphotericin B treatment.</p>
<p>NeXstar currently markets AmBisome in 24 countries, primarily in Europe.</p>
</text>
